intent.readme:
# @tnf-dev/js

## Usage

To use `@tnf-dev/js`, you can import it in your JavaScript or TypeScript files. Here's a simple example:

- Initialize the client:

  ```ts
  import { TeknifyClient } from '@tnf-dev/js';

  const client = new TeknifyClient({
    applicationId: '',
    subscriberId: '',
  });
  ```

- Get all notifications:

  ```ts
  const notifications = await client.notifications.getNotifications();
  console.log(notifications);
  ```

- Mark a notification as read:

  ```ts
  const notificationId = '';
  await client.notifications.markAsRead(notificationId);
  console.log(`Notification ${notificationId} marked as read.`);
  ```

- Listen for new notifications:

  ```ts
  client.notifications.on((notifications) => {
    notifications.forEach((notification) => {
      console.log('New notification:', notification);
    });
  });
  ```

